{
  "id": "u11-l06",
  "unit": "u11-plans",
  "title": "I won't",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**'Won't' = future + না.** Add **না** after the verb, as in the present:\n\n- **যাব** → **যাব না** 'I won't go'\n- **আসবে** → **আসবে না** 'won't come'\n\nDon't use -নি here: **আসেনি** means 'didn't come'.\n\n**দেওয়া** 'give' and **নেওয়া** 'take' have short future stems: **দেব** 'I'll give', **দেবেন** 'you'll give (polite)', **নেব** 'I'll take'. In Bangladesh you'll also hear **দিব, দিবেন, নিব**; both are accepted when you type.\n\nA polite request: **আপনি কি আমাকে একটু পানি দেবেন?** 'Could you give me a little water?' At a shop: **আমি এটা নেব** 'I'll take this one'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "byasto",
      "bn": "ব্যস্ত",
      "tr": "byasto",
      "en": "busy"
    },
    {
      "id": "debo",
      "bn": "দেব",
      "tr": "debo",
      "en": "I will give",
      "notes": "Bangladeshi speech often says দিব (dibo); both are accepted when you type. Also spelled দেবো."
    },
    {
      "id": "deben",
      "bn": "দেবেন",
      "tr": "deben",
      "en": "you (polite) will give",
      "notes": "Also দিবেন (diben) in Bangladeshi speech. আপনি কি আমাকে … দেবেন? is a polite request."
    },
    {
      "id": "nebo",
      "bn": "নেব",
      "tr": "nebo",
      "en": "I will take",
      "notes": "Also নিব (nibo) in Bangladeshi speech. Shopping: আমি এটা নেব 'I'll take this one'."
    }
  ],
